{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generates suggestions for improving code quality while maintaining existing functionality, focusing on readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.py",
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.jsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code for potential improvements. Review for:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Long methods, duplicate code, dead code, magic numbers, deeply nested conditionals, large classes\n2. **Design Patterns**: Opportunities to apply appropriate patterns (Factory, Strategy, Observer, etc.) or anti-patterns to avoid\n3. **Best Practices**: Naming conventions, single responsibility principle, DRY violations, proper error handling, type safety\n4. **Readability**: Complex expressions, unclear variable names, missing comments for complex logic, function length\n5. **Maintainability**: Tight coupling, missing abstractions, hardcoded values, lack of modularity\n6. **Performance**: Unnecessary re-renders (React), inefficient loops, memory leaks, N+1 queries, missing memoization\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions with code examples where helpful. Prioritize suggestions by impact. Maintain existing functionality - suggest improvements, not rewrites."
  }
}